//? Title: C3D:original video frames and visible tensor Adam
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Genuine person-disjoint KTH clips feed all eight3Dconvolutions and five ceil pools. Explicit tensor Adam,complete frame previews and every held-out error expose the limited short fit alongside static and motion references.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.10_3d_and_video_convolutions/c3d.cpp`.

> The method

Preserve original annotated video/person/segment identities,resize actual frames with tensors,and execute the complete compact C3D graph. Show every Adam update,select on validation NLL,restore22 learned arrays for RGB-only inference,and compare complete held-out/temporal-control results.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/c3d_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/c3d_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/c3d_concept.tikz > build/c3d_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/c3d_concept.svg build/c3d_concept.dvi > build/c3d_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
