> Verification and limits

Six native tests check all164signed3Dkernel/bias/input host finite differences,
negative odd-edge pool values/adjoints,the actual full79991015-scalar forward
and every22learned derivative,all1769472decoded/resized source frame pixels
and source identities,every static/motion reference feature/neighbor/metric,
and invalid dropout/geometry contracts. Public examples compile/run and the
original full-check/three-epoch workflow passes. The selected epoch1 has validation NLL1.099830 and held-out NLL1.096773.
Actual selected CNN accuracy is33.3%,below motion1NN66.7%;it predicts
handclapping for all six clips,with recalls0/1/0 and macroF1.166667.
Both accuracies can change substantially with one clip.
The data preview,complete errors and unchanged references constrain any claim
beyond implementation correctness and temporal computation sensitivity.

> Conclusion

The full architecture and every numeric contract execute successfully,but the short custom fit does not outperform the motion reference. Original clips and complete per-clip errors make the report reproducible without a benchmark claim.

> References

- [Tran et al.(2015),Learning Spatiotemporal Features with3DConvolutional Networks](https://arxiv.org/abs/1412.0767).
- [Original KTH action dataset and annotations](https://www.csc.kth.se/cvap/actions/).
- [Pinned original-video mirror](https://huggingface.co/datasets/AtharvaPote/KTH-Action-Recognition-mirror/tree/7076149bdbeff8d70003a68d6291fd080db44683).
